  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare1.WhitneyWontBeHappy": " Whitney won't be happy to see you again after you killed Kelt, but that doesn't matter right now."
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.BreatheInRelief": "[pg]You breathe in relief when you hear Marble's voice, and you tell her of the dream you've just had. The moment you finish explaining to her, she wraps her arms around you in a comforting hug."
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.BringsFaceCloser": ".[sayend][pg]She brings her face closer to yours to share a long, gentle kiss. As your lips separate, you return the hug and she rolls to lay face up, leaving you on top and resting your head on her chest. You can hear her soft breath as it heaves, her heartbeat soothing you and lulling you back to sleep."
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.EyesOpenLet": "Your eyes open as you let out a scream of horror. You are in bed, awakened from a bad dream.[pg]"
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.FallAsleepWarmth": "[pg]You fall asleep in the warmth of each other's embrace."
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.ForYouAndChild": "[saystart]For you, and for our child[if (marbleMultiKids){ren}]"
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.ILoveYou": "[pg][say: I love you, [name].]"
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.SeeEndTogether": "[saystart] We'll see the end together"
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.WhatsWrongSweetie": "[if (silly){[say: What's wrong, sweetie? Did you get another bad end?]|[say: What's wrong, sweetie? Did you have another nightmare?]}]"
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.WhatsWrongSweetieAgain": "[say: What's wrong, sweetie?]"
  "Scenes.Dreams.MarblePureNightmare2.WhispersIntoEar": "[pg][say: It's okay, sweetie. I'm right here,] she whispers into your ear, [say: I'll never leave you.] Marble caresses the back of your head gently. Relaxation washes over you as she runs her fingers over your scalp. [say: You work so hard every day to save Mareth already, you don't need to worry about me. I will take care of myself too,] your eyes are drawn to her large hammer resting against the [bed]."
}
